Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 14:56:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] HTML directionality: :dir() matching, dir=auto cascade hint,
 shadow rules
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Implements 'the directionality' per whatwg/html#9796 and wires it
three ways (the dir-shadow WPT suite pins each edge):

- Node::html_directionality_is_rtl walks the light tree plus the
  shadow-root→host crossing. Slotted nodes do not take HTML
  directionality from their assigned slot even though CSS direction
  inherits through the flat tree (dir-shadow-03: ltr :dir with rtl
  computed on the same element).
- The dir=auto first-strong scan uses assigned nodes when the auto
  element is a slot, light children otherwise; slots met as
  descendants contribute nothing (assigned nodes must not leak into
  shadow-side scans (dir-shadow-30/34), shadow trees are not
  descendants of their host (dir-shadow-33).
- dir=auto resolves into the cascade as a presentational hint on
  direction (its scan exclusions are inexpressible in CSS), so
  getComputedStyle and flat-tree inheritance see the result, and
  author direction rules override it per spec. construct.rs now
  trusts computed direction) the layout-time walk is gone.
- Isolate wrap chars follow computed direction instead of FSI:
  the isolate direction is the element's resolved directionality,
  not first-strong of the rendered stream (a host's shadow text
  must not steer its isolate; dir-shadow-33 ref uses dir=ltr).
